[{:seon.task/name "a-form-has-a-time-bound"
  :seon.task/plan "`seon.turn/act!` evaluates through `seon.repl/eval-string` with no per-form bound, so a model's infinite loop holds its attempt forever. Correct: a config key bounds a form, passed in act!; the interrupt is the named failure point `seon.intr/run` (docs/failure-points.md), and the interrupted form is recorded."
  :seon.task/kind :work
  :seon.task/proofs #{seon.turn-test/an-endless-form-is-interrupted-and-recorded}}
 {:seon.task/name "a-turn-records-what-it-saw-and-spent"
  :seon.task/plan "A turn records its `:seon.turn/basis` and `:seon.turn/split` (`seon.turn/basis!`), but not the model's raw reply, its finish_reason, model and reasoning, nor the whole split as the agent saw it (4-15 s gaps in a real run had to be traced by hand). Correct: per turn, the messages sent are derivable from the basis; the reply's finish_reason, model and reasoning, and the split context render / model round trip / evals / record / tests are recorded. The dashboard's agent page shows the recorded context, not a second producer of it."
  :seon.task/kind :work
  :seon.task/proofs #{seon.turn-test/a-turn-records-its-context-reply-and-time-split}} {:seon.task/name "an-outside-context-is-the-turns-context"
  :seon.task/plan "`seon.turn/context-block` (the server's read of a task for an outside worktree session) now takes the attempt's plan and `seon.turn/observe`'s gaps since the branch's merge base (`seon.merge/uncontracted`), as the turn loop does, so main's pre-existing contract gaps are no longer charged to the agent. It still passes turn n of max-turns 1 to `seon.turn/basis!`, so the context says \"turn 1 of 1\" while the attempt's env says 8. Correct: context-block passes the attempt's env max-turns, so the outside session reads exactly what the turn loop's model would. Replaces the second set of basis arguments; nothing new."
  :seon.task/kind :work
  :seon.task/proofs #{seon.turn-test/an-outside-context-names-only-the-branchs-own-gaps}}
 {:seon.task/name "a-turn-shows-its-cost-against-its-budget"
  :seon.task/plan "Found by worktree dry-run's turn profile (2026-10-23, main 8a901ac3, temporary marks, reverted) and the diagnostics timing audit (notes/timing-audit.md, main checkout): every cost that made a scripted e2e-loop turn 17.7 s against a ~100 ms target grew without any record or check seeing it. Measured spans: test-plan's reach walk 4.3 s (5 plans a turn); merge-main's three-way 4.4 s; the writer's branch-diff 2.6 s (blocking the writer); the octopus merge ~1.6 s; problems/caused 0.37 s; a fresh root's first fork queued 3.8-4.8 s behind the fork server's replay of the boot import (d/with 3,504 ms for 42,942 datoms, then load-changes! 420 ms), visible only as that fork's queue time. What exists: an eval records `:ms` and `:alloc-bytes` (`seon.repl/wrap-cost`), no ticks or CPU; a turn stores `:seon.turn/split` {:context-ms :model-ms :eval-ms :record-ms :tests-ms}, rendered nowhere; spawn, merge, branch-diff, a Flow step and the fork server's replay record no measure as a fact. Correct, in this order (AGENTS §5, docs/cost.md: work is ticks, bytes and calls, exact; wall and CPU are measured, recorded and shown, never red): (1) every eval item carries its ticks (`jolt.host/ticks-of`, 4 ticks overhead, no budget needed) and CPU beside :ms and :alloc-bytes, in `seon.repl/wrap-cost`; (2) the turn's context shows its split and the attempt's against an estimate held as config keys (the turn's own work, apart from the model's wait), each span named; (3) the fork server's replay of a main commit, a spawn, merge-main, branch-diff and the octopus merge each record their datoms, ticks and ms as a fact when they happen, so a regression is an open problem the moment it lands, not a later profile. Proofs: an eval's record carries :ticks; a turn's context shows its split against the estimate; a replay of an n-datom commit records n, ticks and ms."
  :seon.task/kind :work
  :seon.task/proofs #{seon.repl-test/an-evals-record-carries-its-ticks seon.context-test/a-turn-shows-its-split-against-its-estimate seon.fork-server-test/a-replay-records-its-datoms-and-cost}}]
